.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Archrock, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an energy infrastructure company in the United States. The company operates in two segments, Contract Operations and Aftermarket Services. It engages in the designing, sourcing, owning, installing, operating, servicing, repairing, and maintaining of its owned fleet of natural gas compression equipment to provide natural gas compression services. The company also sells over-the-counter parts and components, as well as provides operations, major and routine maintenance, overhaul, and reconfiguration services to customers who own compression equipment. It serves integrated and independent oil and natural gas processors, gatherers, and transporters. Archrock, Inc. was formerly known as Exterran Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to Archrock, Inc. in November 2015. The company was founded in 1990 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. D. Bradley Childers J.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers. Each employee generates $89K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $14K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Archrock, Inc. is a mid-cap energy business with a $4.8B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +21% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 46%.","The business throws off $120M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.93\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 100% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9985775554035317},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $12.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-12244276.62},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 24% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Gross margin tops the Energy peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Growing faster than most Energy peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Financial quality scores above most Energy peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Contrasting Smart Sand (NASDAQ:SND) & Archrock (NYSE:AROC)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/contrasting-smart-sand-nasdaqsnd-archrock-nysearoc.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794547724.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.968,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here is What to Know Beyond Why Archrock, Inc. (AROC) is a Trending Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028498/here-is-what-to-know-beyond-why-archrock-inc-aroc-is-a-trending-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cmost_searched_stocks_v1-3028498","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794488403.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Archrock (AROC) Stock May Still Look Like A Bargain Following The HiVolt Deal","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-aroc/archrock/news/archrock-aroc-s