ve its DCF fair value of $13.70 (margin of safety -100%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 27%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $7.43 to $24.56 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Energy peers: P/FCF 40.1 vs 14.6 (sector median).","The EBIT multiple is close to its own 10-year median (-4%).","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 2.5% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 8.3% (vs the 8% bar).","The 8 covering analysts target $42.38 on average, 55% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 8% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.0%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.28).","It runs a 46% gross margin and converts 8% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 8/9 and cash conversion of 1.93x.","ROE of 22% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.9x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 22pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 1.3% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.8x net debt to EBITDA ($1.6M of cash against $2.4B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 3.6x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.10 in the distress zone."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 20.8% over 3 years, 11.2% over 5 years and 4.1% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 21%).","At current returns, reinvesting 69% of profits supports about 5.3% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -9.3% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are expanding (+3.3% trend).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.01, a backlog worth 57% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 21%.","Capex runs 2.0x depreciation (33.7% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.7%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (6 sales, net $12.2M sold).","It returns 4.4% a year to shareholders (1.5% in buybacks and 3.4% in dividends).","The share count has grown 2.6% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 12 consecutive years, raising it 9.8% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 1,350 employees, each generates about $1.1M of revenue, 0.5x the Energy median, and revenue has fallen 3.3% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $89K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.0M (3x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $14K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":50,"head":"Avoid: priced 100% above its fair value of $13.70.","pros":["Composite 46, above the 39 line (gates 12/26)","Revenue grew 11.2%/yr over 5y","Piotroski F-score 8/9","8 analysts' mean target $42.38 (+55%)","12-1 month momentum +33%"],"cons":["Trades 100% above fair value of $13.70","ROIC 7.7% vs WACC 8.0%","Altman Z in the distress zone (1.10)","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/FCF 40.1x vs sector 14.6x"],"flags":["Priced 100% above its fair value of $13.70","Altman Z in the distress zone (1.10)"],"need":[],"buy_below":11.65,"vc":{"base":13.7,"base_src":"dcf","bear":7.43,"bull":24.56,"alt_median":21.31,"n_alt":2,"gap":-0.4595,"dispersion":0.2655,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","bull case is 3.3x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":13.5876,"ev_ebitda":7.146,"pfcf":14.6331,"pb":1.7432,"roic":0.0952,"gross_margin":0.2462,"fcf_margin":0.0762,"div_yield":0.0357}},"mc_quantiles":[3.77,6.18,7.43,8.55,9.27,9.89,11.01,11.79,12.47,13.43,14.13,14.98,15.92,16.81,17.93,19.26,20.36,21.91,24.56,28.51,34.98],"mc